[] SEGV and BUS signals are usually errors, whereas HUP is not.  That is
[] why nethack saves in the latter case.  When you restore after a SEGV
[] or BUS error, does it usually work?  I suggest including a warning, like
[] "Restoring saved game ...--More--
[]  Game saved after bus error.  Proceed at your own risk."

and the risk of everyone else using the system at that time ...

[] Sometimes nethack saves in a .e file after it catches its own error.
[] These files always seem playable after a restore.  Why not get rid of
[] the .e, and just include the warning.  This would reduce embarassing
[] email to sysadmins.

that would be a reasonable compile option. on my machine (vax/unix) i've
had to recover a few of these error files and they've always worked
(since 2.3e). however, on the mac, for 2.3e these files didn't work.
i haven't had one yet in 3.0 but the point is that they may not always
work so it should be an option. the game should know if it was a panic
save or normal save (not by filename but by a bit in the file) and,
as you suggest, give you a clue when it restores,
(i.e. Restoring panic save file ... vs. Restoring save file ...).

